llcv (2.0.5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Follow the Windows LLCV 2.0.5 update.
  * Customizable keyboard shortcuts (Settings, Guide & logs). All eight
    viewer shortcuts, including Esc, accept a single key or a Ctrl/Alt/Shift
    combination. Duplicate, empty, Super and reserved combinations are
    rejected, and Reset defaults restores the original keys.
  * Keys are matched by scancode, so they work with any input method.
  * Help, menu bar, overlays and settings text show the assigned keys.

 -- Meohong <busimh001@gmail.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0900

llcv (2.0.4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Follow the Windows LLCV 2.0.3 and 2.0.4 updates.
  * Optional 40 fps capture (Video, off by default). It requests 40 fps from
    the driver even when the rate is not in the detected list, confirms the
    rate the driver reports on Start, and shows an error instead of falling
    back to another rate.
  * "Prevent sleep during playback" (App, on by default). Video keeps the
    display and system awake; audio-only lets the display turn off and only
    blocks automatic suspend through the desktop portal. The request is
    released when playback stops or the capture device disconnects. The
    screen saver is no longer blocked on the settings screen.
  * A failed settings save keeps the previous settings file, removes the
    temporary file and shows a notice.
  * The APT source lists only the package architecture, so systems with
    i386 multiarch (for example for Steam) no longer show "doesn't support
    architecture 'i386'" on apt update.

 -- Meohong <busimh001@gmail.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900

llcv (2.0.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * First Linux release, rewritten from the Windows LLCV 2.0.2 design.
  * V4L2 memory-mapped capture with latest-frame-first delivery and
    automatic reconnection.
  * OpenGL 3.3 presentation for NV12, YUY2, MJPEG (libjpeg-turbo) and BGR24.
  * SDL3 audio on PipeWire with the PCM queue target and clock-drift
    correction from the Windows build.
  * Dear ImGui settings screen, diagnostics and audio overlays with
    Korean and English text.
  * P010 (HDR10) capture, HDR10 passthrough through wp_color_management_v1
    on Wayland with a 10-bit framebuffer, and HDR to SDR tone mapping
    (the Windows screenshot curve) on SDR displays and X11.
  * Bundled Dear ImGui 1.92.2b so Debian 13, Ubuntu and Arch build the
    same code.
  * Ubuntu 24.04 support: pinned SDL3 3.4.18 linked statically through the
    pkg.llcv.bundled-sdl3 build profile, and a bundled color-management
    protocol file for older wayland-protocols.
  * The app states when HDR input or output is not supported, and why.
  * Alt shows a menu bar with the viewer commands.
  * NVIDIA VSR, WASAPI Exclusive and ASIO are not available on Linux.

 -- Meohong <busimh001@gmail.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
